// PURE-CEDAR PARALLEL to 1036 (int for entity). An ordinary Cedar `when`
// equality: `context.input.mode` on Tool2 is declared an enum entity type
// `Drupe::Tool2_Input_mode`, compared with `==` against the integer
// literal `5`. An int is not an entity, so Cedar's strict-mode validator is
// expected to reject the comparison as ill-typed.
//
// This exercises the base Cedar validation path (not the temporal dialect's
// type-checker), establishing whether the int-for-entity gap seen in 1036 is
// specific to the temporal sublanguage.
//
// Expected: rejected at `validate` (by Cedar's own validator).
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Tool2", resource)
when { context.input.mode == 5 };
